# NexStay Laravel Coding Rules

## Architecture Mandate

NexStay is a **Modular Monolith**. Business logic lives in `app/Domain/{Module}/`. Controllers are thin. Do not put business logic in controllers, models, or route closures.

```
Request → Controller (validate) → Action::execute() → Response
                                       ↓
                                  Services / Models / Events
```

## Action Classes

Every business operation is an Action class. One action = one operation.

```php
// ✅ CORRECT
namespace App\Domain\HBMS\Actions;

class CheckInGuest
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly FolioService $folioService
    ) {}

    public function execute(Reservation $reservation, array $options = []): Folio
    {
        return DB::transaction(function () use ($reservation, $options) {
            // ... business logic here
        });
    }
}

// ✅ Controller calls the action — nothing else
class ReservationController extends Controller
{
    public function checkIn(CheckInRequest $request, Reservation $reservation): JsonResponse
    {
        $folio = app(CheckInGuest::class)->execute($reservation, $request->validated());
        return FolioResource::make($folio)->response();
    }
}

// ❌ NEVER — business logic in controller
class ReservationController extends Controller
{
    public function checkIn(Request $request, Reservation $reservation): JsonResponse
    {
        $reservation->update(['status' => 'checked_in']); // NO
        $folio = Folio::create([...]); // NO
        return response()->json($folio);
    }
}
```

## Money — Always `brick/money`

**Never use floats or plain integers for monetary values.**

```php
use Brick\Money\Money;
use Brick\Math\RoundingMode;

// ✅ CORRECT
$price     = Money::of('15000.00', 'TZS');
$tax       = $price->multipliedBy('0.18', RoundingMode::HALF_UP);
$total     = $price->plus($tax);
$stored    = $total->getAmount()->toFloat(); // only when writing to DB

// ❌ NEVER
$price = 15000.00;
$tax   = $price * 0.18;  // float arithmetic on money = data corruption
```

## Database Transactions — Always on Financial Operations

Any code touching folios, payments, till_sessions, or till_movements must be wrapped.

```php
// ✅ CORRECT
DB::transaction(function () use ($folio, $order) {
    $this->folioService->postCharge($folio, 'restaurant', $order->total);
    $order->update(['status' => 'closed']);
    TillMovement::create([...]);
});

// ❌ NEVER — partial writes on failure = corrupted folio
$this->folioService->postCharge($folio, 'restaurant', $order->total);
$order->update(['status' => 'closed']); // if this fails, folio is wrong
```

## Eloquent Rules

```php
// ✅ Always eager-load to prevent N+1
Reservation::with(['guest', 'room.roomType', 'folio.transactions'])->get();

// ✅ Use select() in production queries
Reservation::select('id', 'booking_ref', 'status', 'check_in_date')
    ->where('status', 'confirmed')
    ->get();

// ✅ Soft deletes on all domain models
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\SoftDeletes;
class Reservation extends Model
{
    use SoftDeletes;
}

// ❌ NEVER — raw string interpolation in queries
DB::select("SELECT * FROM reservations WHERE id = '$id'"); // SQL injection

// ✅ ALWAYS — use bindings
DB::select('SELECT * FROM reservations WHERE id = ?', [$id]);
```

## FormRequest — Always

Every API write operation uses a FormRequest. No `$request->all()` in controllers.

```php
// ✅ CORRECT
class CreateReservationRequest extends FormRequest
{
    public function rules(): array
    {
        return [
            'guest_id'       => ['required', 'uuid', 'exists:guests,id'],
            'check_in_date'  => ['required', 'date', 'after_or_equal:today'],
            'check_out_date' => ['required', 'date', 'after:check_in_date'],
            'adults'         => ['required', 'integer', 'min:1', 'max:10'],
        ];
    }
}

// ❌ NEVER
public function store(Request $request)
{
    $data = $request->all(); // unvalidated, dangerous
}
```

## Model Conventions

```php
class Room extends Model
{
    use SoftDeletes;

    // Always explicit fillable — never $guarded = []
    protected $fillable = ['room_type_id', 'room_number', 'floor', 'status'];

    // Cast JSON columns
    protected $casts = [
        'amenities' => 'array',
        'photos'    => 'array',
    ];

    // UUID primary key setup
    public $incrementing = false;
    protected $keyType   = 'string';

    protected static function booted(): void
    {
        static::creating(fn ($model) => $model->id ??= (string) Str::uuid());
    }
}
```

## Events & Listeners

Domain events decouple side effects from core business logic.

```php
// Fire events for significant domain moments
GuestCheckedIn::dispatch($reservation, $room, $folio);
OrderFiredToKds::dispatch($order, $items);
TillSessionClosed::dispatch($session, $overShort);

// Listeners handle side effects
class SendCheckInConfirmation
{
    public function handle(GuestCheckedIn $event): void
    {
        // send email/SMS — this is a side effect, not core logic
    }
}
```

## Error Handling

```php
// Domain exceptions for business rule violations
throw new \DomainException('Reservation is not in confirmed status.');

// Custom exception classes for typed catching
throw new TillNotOpenException($outletId);
throw new InsufficientStockException($item, $required, $available);

// Use abort() only in controllers for HTTP errors
abort(403, 'You do not have permission to void this transaction.');
```

## Naming Conventions

| Thing | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Action classes | Verb + Noun | `CheckInGuest`, `RecordCashPayment`, `RunNightAudit` |
| Service classes | Noun + Service | `FolioService`, `TaxService`, `KdsService` |
| Events | Past tense | `GuestCheckedIn`, `OrderFiredToKds`, `TillSessionClosed` |
| Jobs | Verb phrase | `SyncAvailabilityToOta`, `FiscalizePayment` |
| Requests | Action + Request | `CreateReservationRequest`, `RecordCashPaymentRequest` |
| Controllers | Noun + Controller | `ReservationController`, `TillSessionController` |
| Resources | Noun + Resource | `ReservationResource`, `FolioResource` |

## Artisan Commands

Custom commands live in `app/Console/Commands/` and are prefixed `nexstay:`.

```php
// php artisan nexstay:night-audit
// php artisan nexstay:sync-ota
// php artisan nexstay:rebuild-availability
// php artisan tenants:create {name} {slug}
```

## Security Checklist (Every Feature)

- [ ] FormRequest validation on all inputs
- [ ] `permission:` middleware on sensitive routes
- [ ] No raw SQL string interpolation
- [ ] Financial operations wrapped in `DB::transaction()`
- [ ] Sensitive model fields encrypted (`id_number`, `date_of_birth`)
- [ ] Activity log on financial model mutations
- [ ] Webhook inputs verified via HMAC before processing
